commit 8606832fa6eb2d2e307b6815252da3cbb25fac15
Author: lora-dataset-studio <noreply@lora-dataset-studio.dev>
Date:   Sun Aug 2 13:59:21 2026 +0200

    feat(upscale): add SeedVR2 as the fidelity alternative to Klein improve
    
    Idea and specification by SurpassHR (GitHub #32): Klein's improve pass is a
    diffusion edit, so it re-renders skin and micro-detail and can move colour —
    the wrong trade when the frame's exact look is what the dataset teaches.
    SeedVR2 (ByteDance-Seed, Apache-2.0) restores detail instead of reinterpreting
    it. Both are now offered on the same pass, and every surface states the
    difference in one line so nobody discovers it on a ruined batch.
    
    * backend/app/services/seedvr2_helper.py — the engine: resolvers over the
      models/SEEDVR2 folder, missing/invalid-asset and node-pack preflight, the
      ComfyUI graph, and the enqueue. Node ids are read from the pack's own
      define_schema (SeedVR2VideoUpscaler), not its README, which spells them
      differently and would have made every preflight report a missing node on a
      correct install.
    * Only builds already ON DISK are ever submitted: the pack's loaders download
      an unknown name on first use, and a dropdown must not start a multi-gigabyte
      download.
    * The node pack is deliberately NOT auto-installed, unlike comfyui-krea2edit:
      it declares thirteen pip dependencies that belong in ComfyUI's interpreter,
      which this app does not own. Setup downloads the two weights (3.9 GB) and
      names ComfyUI-Manager for the pack.
    * Settings > Image engines: DiT build, target resolution, max long edge, colour
      correction, block swapping, and the default engine for the improve pass. No
      batch-size knob on purpose — the node's batch size is a video window whose
      frames share attention, so grouping unrelated photos would let them bleed
      into each other. The card says so rather than shipping a dial that corrupts.
    * Bulk actions: one button per available engine on the selection, each stating
      its trade-off; the batch choice never comes from the setting.
    
    Stored ids are untouched: derivation_kind stays klein_image_improve and action
    stays upscale_improve, with the engine recorded additively, so every existing
    improved tile keeps curating, undoing and re-improving as before.
    
    30 new backend tests + 7 new frontend contract tests.
